Test-only capability services for tests/sys/mac_capability:

  keystore/     mac_capability_test_keystore    async key-value store
  kernelstore/  mac_capability_test_kernelstore sync shared key-value store
  cleanup/      mac_capability_test_cleanup     unload/cleanup ordering probe
  include/      wire protocols shared with the test programs

They are built by buildkernel from sys/modules/mac_capability_test_* when
tests are enabled (MK_TESTS), installed in /boot/kernel and packaged in
mac-capability-tests, never in a kernel package.  Production code does not
include their headers.

The keystore and kernelstore cases declare require.kmods; preload both in
the test guest's /boot/loader.conf:

  mac_capability_test_keystore_load="YES"
  mac_capability_test_kernelstore_load="YES"

The unload and cleanup cases load and unload mac_capability_test_cleanup
themselves, so it must not be preloaded.  The fixtures register test
services; load them only in a disposable test guest, never on a host whose
capability plane is in production use.
